WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.460
Pathway to Revival.

00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:05.980
As I've had the opportunity to preach those two messages

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:08.699
in the last couple of weeks of Pathway to Revival,

00:00:08.699 --> 00:00:13.380
I have mentioned to you that really the subject of humility

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:17.379
is seen in the text of Scripture as bookends

00:00:17.379 --> 00:00:21.379
to the instruction that is provided in verses seven,

00:00:21.379 --> 00:00:22.659
eight, and nine.

00:00:22.659 --> 00:00:24.819
In verse number six, the Bible says,

00:00:24.819 --> 00:00:26.899
but he giveth more grace,

00:00:26.899 --> 00:00:30.760
wherefore he saith, God resisteth the proud,

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:33.500
but giveth grace unto the humble.

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:35.919
Then we find in verse seven, eight, and nine,

00:00:35.919 --> 00:00:37.580
the six steps, if you will,

00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:41.340
Pathway to Revival followed by verse number 10,

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:42.180
where the Bible says,

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:45.380
humble yourselves in the sight of the Lord,

00:00:45.380 --> 00:00:48.139
and he shall lift you up.

00:00:48.139 --> 00:00:50.560
I believe that the emphasis of humility

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:53.900
is placed as bookends to this instruction,

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:56.880
because the reality is if we do not humble ourselves,

00:00:57.659 --> 00:00:59.520
we will not follow the instruction.

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:01.639
If we're prideful and arrogant people,

00:01:01.639 --> 00:01:04.400
we're not going to submit ourselves to God.

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:06.040
We're not going to resist the devil

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:07.800
and the power of God's might.

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:09.800
We're not gonna see him flee from us,

00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:12.800
that promise that is given in verse number seven.

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:15.360
We're not gonna draw nigh to God.

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:18.000
We're not going to have the process,

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:21.040
as we spoke of in verse number eight last week,

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:22.959
of examination, because why?

00:01:22.959 --> 00:01:24.779
We think we're okay.

00:01:24.779 --> 00:01:25.980
We're full of pride.

00:01:26.860 --> 00:01:29.360
There's no need for me to examine myself.

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:31.819
There's no need for me to get alone with God,

00:01:31.819 --> 00:01:34.059
because I'm prideful, I'm arrogant.

00:01:34.059 --> 00:01:36.160
I think everything's good.

00:01:37.339 --> 00:01:40.500
So we'll not take that fourth step of examination,

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:43.019
which leads to the fifth step of brokenness,

00:01:43.019 --> 00:01:46.819
to acknowledging our sin and confessing our sin

00:01:46.819 --> 00:01:50.300
before our gracious, loving God,

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:52.300
and we find that it will not lead

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:55.180
to that repentance and restoration.

00:01:55.180 --> 00:01:57.620
And so as we come to the subject here this morning

00:01:57.620 --> 00:02:00.900
and kind of wrap up this section of James

00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:03.860
in this fourth chapter, we see the emphasis,

00:02:03.860 --> 00:02:06.819
and I've simply titled the message this morning there

00:02:06.819 --> 00:02:10.899
from verse number 10, humble yourselves.

00:02:10.899 --> 00:02:13.179
It was kind of interesting, because in verse number seven,

00:02:13.179 --> 00:02:15.740
and I belabored the point a few weeks ago,

00:02:15.740 --> 00:02:20.380
when the Bible said, submit yourselves, therefore, to God.

00:02:20.380 --> 00:02:23.259
And we mentioned, as we looked at that verse of Scripture,

00:02:23.259 --> 00:02:25.860
that it is a personal decision.

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:28.460
It's something that I cannot do for you,

00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:30.220
and you cannot do for me.

00:02:30.220 --> 00:02:34.699
This idea of submitting yourselves, therefore, to God.

00:02:34.699 --> 00:02:37.020
But we see in verse number 10,

00:02:37.020 --> 00:02:39.460
the Bible says humble yourselves,

00:02:39.460 --> 00:02:42.339
and we've used it as our title this morning for our message,

00:02:42.339 --> 00:02:45.979
and the reality is that I cannot be humble for you,

00:02:45.979 --> 00:02:48.100
and you cannot be humble for me.

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:50.619
It is something that each of us as individuals

00:02:50.619 --> 00:02:53.619
must ensure that we walk in humility,

00:02:53.619 --> 00:02:57.339
that as Peter would say, that we're clothed with humility.

00:02:57.339 --> 00:02:59.419
And we find that the instruction here

00:02:59.419 --> 00:03:02.940
is humble yourselves in the sight of the Lord,

00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:06.020
and he shall lift you up.

00:03:06.020 --> 00:03:07.699
The subject of pride and humility

00:03:07.699 --> 00:03:10.300
is addressed throughout the Scriptures.

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:11.619
As you study the Scriptures,

00:03:11.619 --> 00:03:16.619
you find that pride is at the heart of Lucifer's rebellion.

00:03:16.619 --> 00:03:19.979
I will, he says five different times.

00:03:19.979 --> 00:03:23.100
We find that it led him to being cast out of heaven,

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:27.339
and we understand, as you were to read Isaiah and Ezekiel

00:03:27.339 --> 00:03:29.899
referencing that particular event,

00:03:29.899 --> 00:03:33.899
and we see that pride is at the heart of his rebellion.

00:03:33.899 --> 00:03:35.860
We're told, as we study the Scriptures,

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:37.839
that God hates pride.

00:03:37.839 --> 00:03:40.619
We're told right here in the text of Scripture,

00:03:40.619 --> 00:03:44.380
in verse number six, that God resists the proud.

00:03:45.380 --> 00:03:49.380
Solomon reminds us, as you study through

00:03:49.380 --> 00:03:54.100
the book of Proverbs, that pride is the root of contention,

00:03:55.300 --> 00:03:58.740
and that pride brings destruction.

00:03:58.740 --> 00:04:01.000
Countless are those throughout the ages

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:03.940
who have been deceived by pride.

00:04:03.940 --> 00:04:06.160
See, pride is deceptive.

00:04:06.160 --> 00:04:09.020
And we find that Solomon mentions

00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:10.860
about pride bringing contention,

00:04:10.860 --> 00:04:13.139
that pride leads to destruction.

00:04:13.259 --> 00:04:15.100
It says this in Proverbs 11 too,

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:18.820
when pride cometh, then cometh shame.

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:21.579
There's nothing good about pride.

00:04:22.779 --> 00:04:24.119
Nothing good about pride.

00:04:25.100 --> 00:04:28.299
We could read and we could speak about Saul,

00:04:28.299 --> 00:04:31.899
and how Saul was, when he was little in his sight,

00:04:31.899 --> 00:04:34.660
but then when he got full of himself,

00:04:34.660 --> 00:04:37.179
and how he disobeyed the instruction of God

00:04:37.179 --> 00:04:39.299
through Samuel the prophet.

00:04:39.299 --> 00:04:41.260
You can read of that portion of Scripture,

00:04:41.260 --> 00:04:45.320
and you can see just the shame that was brought

00:04:45.320 --> 00:04:47.059
because of pride, the destruction,

00:04:47.059 --> 00:04:49.980
the rejection because of pride.

00:04:49.980 --> 00:04:52.179
Pride led him to a place of disobedience,

00:04:52.179 --> 00:04:54.619
led him to a place of self-sufficiency.

00:04:54.619 --> 00:04:57.279
You can think about Uzziah, great king.

00:04:57.279 --> 00:04:59.500
I mean, God used him in such a great way,

00:04:59.500 --> 00:05:02.079
and you can see all of the wonderful things,

00:05:02.079 --> 00:05:04.660
but the Bible tells us that when he was lifted up,

00:05:04.660 --> 00:05:06.519
when he was strong in his own eyes,

00:05:06.519 --> 00:05:09.540
when he was in that position of having that pride

00:05:09.540 --> 00:05:12.100
and that arrogancy, he goes into the temple

00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:13.779
and tries to fulfill the role

00:05:13.779 --> 00:05:16.339
that was reserved for the priest,

00:05:17.380 --> 00:05:18.579
and he becomes a leper.

00:05:19.940 --> 00:05:21.500
Pride.

00:05:21.500 --> 00:05:23.260
Could read of Nebuchadnezzar.

00:05:24.339 --> 00:05:27.980
This man, of course, the king of Babylon,

00:05:27.980 --> 00:05:30.519
and all of the might and all of the power

00:05:30.519 --> 00:05:34.299
and all that he had, and you find that he could walk through

00:05:34.299 --> 00:05:38.220
and speak of Babylon and all that he had been able

00:05:38.220 --> 00:05:41.820
to accomplish, but he learned in a very real way

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:43.980
that God is able to humble.

00:05:45.380 --> 00:05:49.579
We can think of example after example of those

00:05:49.579 --> 00:05:54.579
that have faced great shame and destruction because of pride.

00:05:54.579 --> 00:05:57.480
Pride is defined this way.

00:05:57.480 --> 00:06:00.459
Pride is inordinate self-esteem.

00:06:01.600 --> 00:06:06.600
An unreasonable conceit of one's own superiority

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:11.880
in talents, beauty, wealth, accomplishments,

00:06:12.859 --> 00:06:15.839
rank, or elevation in office.

00:06:16.799 --> 00:06:21.359
It manifests itself this way, in lofty airs,

00:06:21.359 --> 00:06:26.359
distance, reserve, and often in contempt of others.

00:06:28.440 --> 00:06:33.440
That's how pride is defined in 1828 Noah Webster's dictionary.

00:06:33.519 --> 00:06:35.200
We think of the word arrogant.

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:37.200
We think of the word haughty.

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:42.200
We see the pride that is so prevalent in our society today.

00:06:43.160 --> 00:06:46.459
We think about pride in such high offices today.

00:06:46.459 --> 00:06:50.200
We think about people that walk around proud,

00:06:51.239 --> 00:06:53.140
just full of themselves.

00:06:54.140 --> 00:06:56.480
I believe this morning as you study the scriptures

00:06:56.480 --> 00:07:00.019
that pride is a characteristic of these last days.

00:07:00.019 --> 00:07:02.920
In fact, Paul said it this way in 2 Timothy 3,

00:07:02.920 --> 00:07:03.920
in verse number two,

00:07:03.920 --> 00:07:07.839
for men shall be lovers of their own selves.

00:07:07.839 --> 00:07:08.679
Now think about that.

00:07:08.679 --> 00:07:10.119
That's pride right there from the beginning.

00:07:10.119 --> 00:07:12.440
They're lovers of their own selves.

00:07:12.440 --> 00:07:14.820
And then it says this, covetous.

00:07:14.820 --> 00:07:18.760
What is it that makes them to covet is that pride.

00:07:18.760 --> 00:07:20.279
They're lovers of their own selves.

00:07:20.279 --> 00:07:21.839
It says that they're boasters.

00:07:21.839 --> 00:07:22.799
Think about that.

00:07:22.799 --> 00:07:25.959
Boasting, that's the manifestation of pride.

00:07:25.959 --> 00:07:27.959
He then says proud.

00:07:27.959 --> 00:07:31.040
And yes, it's contained right there in 2 Timothy 3

00:07:31.040 --> 00:07:32.079
in verse number two.

00:07:32.079 --> 00:07:33.079
They're blasphemers.

00:07:33.079 --> 00:07:34.059
They curse God.

00:07:34.059 --> 00:07:36.040
They lift their hand against God.

00:07:36.040 --> 00:07:38.720
And we find that it says they're disobedient to parents,

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:40.420
unthankful, unholy.

00:07:40.420 --> 00:07:44.220
That's how Paul begins to describe the last days

00:07:44.220 --> 00:07:46.820
in 2 Timothy 3 in verse number two.

00:07:47.839 --> 00:07:52.480
And we see this morning that pride, it's prevalent today.

00:07:52.480 --> 00:07:54.660
We see it all around.

00:07:54.660 --> 00:07:58.799
But the idea is not so much that we are to identify pride

00:07:58.799 --> 00:08:00.440
in the life of someone else,

00:08:00.440 --> 00:08:04.679
for the scriptures say humble yourselves.

00:08:04.679 --> 00:08:08.119
The reality this morning is that oftentimes it's easy for us

00:08:08.119 --> 00:08:11.320
to identify pride in someone else's life

00:08:11.320 --> 00:08:13.760
rather than in our own life.

00:08:13.760 --> 00:08:16.519
And oftentimes as we think about the truth

00:08:16.519 --> 00:08:20.339
of 1 Corinthians chapter 11, let a man examine himself,

00:08:20.339 --> 00:08:23.119
that oftentimes we'd like to be in the place

00:08:23.119 --> 00:08:27.260
of examining someone else rather than examining ourselves.

00:08:28.260 --> 00:08:32.739
And though we can identify pride in the lives of others,

00:08:32.739 --> 00:08:37.739
the scriptures admonish and instruct us to humble ourselves.

00:08:38.979 --> 00:08:43.099
I would say this morning that pride adversely affects

00:08:43.099 --> 00:08:47.359
our fellowship with the redeemed, with one another.

00:08:47.359 --> 00:08:50.179
You think about how pride can cause contention.

00:08:50.179 --> 00:08:53.380
We know only by pride cometh contention.

00:08:53.380 --> 00:08:55.619
And you think about the contention and you think about

00:08:55.619 --> 00:08:59.659
the way in which pride can adversely affect fellowship

00:08:59.659 --> 00:09:02.099
within the family of God.

00:09:03.979 --> 00:09:06.179
But we're most concerned this morning

00:09:06.179 --> 00:09:08.979
how pride will adversely affect our relationship,

00:09:08.979 --> 00:09:11.700
or our fellowship with our Redeemer.

00:09:11.700 --> 00:09:13.419
See the Bible says very plainly

00:09:13.419 --> 00:09:16.900
that God resisteth the proud.

00:09:16.900 --> 00:09:19.260
And this morning when we understand the portion

00:09:19.260 --> 00:09:21.340
of scripture that we're looking at and understand

00:09:21.340 --> 00:09:25.099
the subject of pride and humility and understand

00:09:25.380 --> 00:09:30.140
that my fellowship with my Redeemer is adversely affected

00:09:30.140 --> 00:09:32.440
when I walk and live in pride.

00:09:34.940 --> 00:09:38.820
Understanding these biblical truths ought to cause

00:09:38.820 --> 00:09:43.099
each one of us this morning to do exactly what James says

00:09:43.099 --> 00:09:48.099
in verse 10 of chapter four, humble yourselves.

00:09:48.140 --> 00:09:51.539
When we look at all of the biblical truth with regard

00:09:51.539 --> 00:09:54.400
to the subject of pride and humility,

00:09:54.760 --> 00:09:56.960
and when we look at the case studies of those

00:09:56.960 --> 00:10:00.000
that have gone before us that have faced shame and.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:03.519
destruction, because of pride, it ought to cause us to say,

00:10:03.519 --> 00:10:05.519
I want to stay away from that.

00:10:05.519 --> 00:10:09.979
I don't want to be prideful.

00:10:09.979 --> 00:10:13.680
When we understand fellowship and contention that

00:10:13.680 --> 00:10:18.680
comes as a result of that pride in the heart and the life

00:10:18.680 --> 00:10:21.399
of God's people, we should say, man, I don't want that.

00:10:21.399 --> 00:10:26.120
When I understand that God says he resisteth the proud,

00:10:26.120 --> 00:10:28.600
but he giveth grace unto the humble,

00:10:28.600 --> 00:10:30.459
I don't think any one of us this morning,

00:10:30.459 --> 00:10:32.520
when we look at these biblical truths

00:10:32.520 --> 00:10:35.159
and we try to kind of summarize them all together,

00:10:35.159 --> 00:10:37.840
I don't think any one of us in our right mind

00:10:37.840 --> 00:10:39.200
would leave here this morning and say,

00:10:39.200 --> 00:10:41.200
I think I'm gonna keep walking in pride.

00:10:42.799 --> 00:10:44.099
It'd be foolish.

00:10:45.959 --> 00:10:49.200
Again, Peter said that we're to be clothed with humility.

00:10:49.200 --> 00:10:51.540
It's interesting in 1 Peter chapter five,

00:10:51.540 --> 00:10:54.040
that Peter references exactly what we see here

00:10:54.040 --> 00:10:57.599
in chapter four in verse number six of the book of James.

00:10:57.599 --> 00:10:59.200
The Bible says, likewise ye younger,

00:10:59.200 --> 00:11:00.639
submit yourselves unto the elder,

00:11:00.639 --> 00:11:03.220
yea, all of you be subject one to another,

00:11:03.220 --> 00:11:06.040
and be clothed with humility,

00:11:06.040 --> 00:11:11.040
for God resisteth the proud and giveth grace to the humble.

00:11:12.260 --> 00:11:13.540
Do you think God wants us to know

00:11:13.540 --> 00:11:15.599
what he thinks about pride?

00:11:15.599 --> 00:11:17.760
I mean, he makes it abundantly clear, doesn't he?

00:11:17.760 --> 00:11:19.000
I mean, he holds nothing back.

00:11:19.000 --> 00:11:23.160
He makes it so obvious that he hates pride

00:11:23.160 --> 00:11:25.800
and that he resists the proud.

00:11:25.800 --> 00:11:28.199
So understanding all of these things this morning,

00:11:28.199 --> 00:11:33.080
I believe that pride must be identified in our lives,

00:11:33.080 --> 00:11:34.720
in my life and in your life,

00:11:34.720 --> 00:11:37.040
and then pride must be rooted out.

00:11:37.959 --> 00:11:41.239
Pride must be identified and then rooted out.

00:11:41.239 --> 00:11:44.720
By the way, having a false sense of humility

00:11:44.720 --> 00:11:47.639
is really just pride wrapped in a different way.

00:11:49.120 --> 00:11:51.519
God has gifted his people.

00:11:51.519 --> 00:11:55.000
God has provided, the Bible says,

00:11:55.040 --> 00:11:57.040
every man hath received the gift,

00:11:57.040 --> 00:11:59.639
even so let him minister one to another.

00:11:59.639 --> 00:12:01.400
And we understand that we're to be good stewards

00:12:01.400 --> 00:12:03.760
of the manifold grace of God.

00:12:03.760 --> 00:12:07.239
And so it's this idea with regard to pride

00:12:07.239 --> 00:12:10.240
and seeking to identify and root out pride.

00:12:10.240 --> 00:12:12.160
And really the question this morning is,

00:12:12.160 --> 00:12:14.039
how do we do that?

00:12:14.039 --> 00:12:15.800
How do we identify pride in our lives?

00:12:15.800 --> 00:12:17.320
How do we root it out of our lives?

00:12:17.320 --> 00:12:20.039
Because so often, if we're not careful,

00:12:20.039 --> 00:12:21.619
and even as we look at the scriptures,

00:12:21.619 --> 00:12:25.419
it's so easy to get full of ourselves.

00:12:25.419 --> 00:12:30.259
It's so easy to get, as we use that terminology, a big head.

00:12:30.259 --> 00:12:31.699
Listen, we can get prideful

00:12:31.699 --> 00:12:33.899
about being right on biblical truth.

00:12:34.740 --> 00:12:36.080
We can become prideful.

00:12:37.020 --> 00:12:40.500
Instead of recognizing that God has been gracious to us

00:12:40.500 --> 00:12:43.740
and allowed us to know the truth of the word of God.

00:12:43.740 --> 00:12:47.139
And through that, giving us the truth of the word of God,

00:12:47.139 --> 00:12:48.660
it should not lead to pride,

00:12:48.660 --> 00:12:52.020
but it should lead to an understanding of responsibility

00:12:52.020 --> 00:12:54.059
of being able to take that very truth

00:12:54.059 --> 00:12:55.720
and share it with other people.

00:12:56.899 --> 00:12:58.500
But if we're not careful at times,

00:12:58.500 --> 00:13:00.699
we can get so prideful and so arrogant,

00:13:00.699 --> 00:13:03.619
even in right positions.

00:13:03.619 --> 00:13:05.779
And so this morning, how do we deal with pride?

00:13:05.779 --> 00:13:06.940
How do we identify it?

00:13:06.940 --> 00:13:08.259
How do we root it out?

00:13:08.259 --> 00:13:09.940
Two simple thoughts this morning

00:13:09.940 --> 00:13:11.960
that I hope will be helpful for us.

00:13:11.960 --> 00:13:14.419
Notice right here in verse number 10,

00:13:14.419 --> 00:13:19.419
the Bible says, humble yourselves in the sight of the Lord

00:13:19.779 --> 00:13:23.059
and he shall lift you up.

00:13:23.059 --> 00:13:26.139
I believe the first step in helping us to identify

00:13:26.139 --> 00:13:28.419
and root out pride in our lives

00:13:28.419 --> 00:13:31.899
is to have a proper view of God.

00:13:31.899 --> 00:13:33.820
A proper view of God.

00:13:33.820 --> 00:13:37.740
See, so many things in our lives are hindered

00:13:37.740 --> 00:13:40.339
when we do not have a proper view of God.

00:13:40.339 --> 00:13:42.619
When we do not see God as he really is.

00:13:43.020 --> 00:13:45.759
See, what has happened, Romans chapter number one

00:13:45.759 --> 00:13:47.500
talks about bringing God down

00:13:47.500 --> 00:13:50.940
to a human kind of a perspective.

00:13:50.940 --> 00:13:54.899
And we understand that we live in a world

00:13:54.899 --> 00:13:59.419
where they seek to bring God down to man's level.

00:13:59.419 --> 00:14:01.399
But our God transcends us.

00:14:02.320 --> 00:14:05.779
Our God is perfect and he's holy and he's righteous.

00:14:05.779 --> 00:14:07.580
And we begin to think this morning

00:14:07.580 --> 00:14:11.300
about the importance of having a proper view of God.

00:14:11.300 --> 00:14:13.520
And how do we get that proper view of God?

00:14:13.520 --> 00:14:16.260
Well, we get it by having a proper relationship

00:14:16.260 --> 00:14:17.660
with the word of God.

00:14:17.660 --> 00:14:19.260
Because it's through the word of God

00:14:19.260 --> 00:14:21.660
that we understand who God is.

00:14:21.660 --> 00:14:24.540
I cannot have a proper understanding,

00:14:24.540 --> 00:14:29.299
I cannot have a proper view of God apart from this book.

00:14:29.299 --> 00:14:32.600
In fact, many people have tried to summarize

00:14:32.600 --> 00:14:36.579
and give in their minds who God is and what God is like

00:14:36.579 --> 00:14:40.700
and they do it void of this precious book, the Bible,

00:14:40.700 --> 00:14:44.019
and they come up with all kinds of wrong conclusions.

00:14:45.299 --> 00:14:48.059
Yesterday, as I was speaking with that lady

00:14:48.059 --> 00:14:49.640
sharing the gospel with her,

00:14:49.640 --> 00:14:52.579
I asked her as I went to Matthew 16,

00:14:52.579 --> 00:14:56.540
and I said, the most important question is who is Jesus?

00:14:56.540 --> 00:15:00.980
She said, well, he's the greatest rabbi that ever lived.

00:15:00.980 --> 00:15:03.880
And I said, you know, he never even claimed to be a rabbi.

00:15:06.700 --> 00:15:08.940
See, that's just a title that someone gave to him.

00:15:08.940 --> 00:15:10.220
By the way, the rabbis of the day

00:15:10.720 --> 00:15:13.019
didn't think he was the greatest rabbi that ever lived.

00:15:13.019 --> 00:15:13.859
Right?

00:15:13.859 --> 00:15:16.700
And here's the reality, he's a great teacher,

00:15:16.700 --> 00:15:19.339
he's the greatest one that ever taught.

00:15:19.339 --> 00:15:21.899
But the reality is that he's God.

00:15:21.899 --> 00:15:23.700
He's God.

00:15:23.700 --> 00:15:26.140
And so we begin to understand this morning

00:15:26.140 --> 00:15:28.779
that if I'm really going to humble myself,

00:15:28.779 --> 00:15:32.540
notice the Bible says, in the sight of the Lord,

00:15:32.540 --> 00:15:35.540
that I take that position that I understand this morning

00:15:35.540 --> 00:15:37.339
that I must have a proper view of God.

00:15:37.339 --> 00:15:39.480
Look at Isaiah chapter six, if you will.

00:15:39.480 --> 00:15:42.760
It's really kind of the classic passage of scripture

00:15:42.760 --> 00:15:46.239
that we would go to with regard to seeing God

00:15:46.239 --> 00:15:47.679
in his rightful place.

00:15:47.679 --> 00:15:49.399
And we find that here, it's interesting,

00:15:49.399 --> 00:15:52.239
I mentioned about Uzziah by way of introduction.

00:15:52.239 --> 00:15:54.920
And the Bible tells us here in Isaiah chapter number six

00:15:54.920 --> 00:15:58.600
that it was in the year that King Uzziah died.

00:15:58.600 --> 00:16:00.920
And so at that same time, when you think about Uzziah,

00:16:00.920 --> 00:16:02.679
and you think about how God used him

00:16:02.679 --> 00:16:06.000
and how God advanced the kingdom under his leadership,

00:16:06.000 --> 00:16:08.959
but then how he was lifted up with pride

00:16:09.480 --> 00:16:12.920
and how he took responsibilities that were not his to take.

00:16:12.920 --> 00:16:16.640
And we find here that in that very year that Uzziah died,

00:16:16.640 --> 00:16:21.640
notice what Isaiah says, I saw also the Lord

00:16:21.839 --> 00:16:26.760
sitting upon a throne, high and lifted up

00:16:26.760 --> 00:16:30.839
and his train filled the temple.

00:16:30.839 --> 00:16:34.839
Above it stood the seraphims, each one had six wings.

00:16:34.839 --> 00:16:36.399
With twain he covered his face

00:16:36.399 --> 00:16:37.760
and with twain he covered his feet

00:16:37.760 --> 00:16:40.359
and with twain he did fly.

00:16:40.359 --> 00:16:42.559
And one cried unto another and said,

00:16:42.559 --> 00:16:47.559
holy, holy, holy is the Lord of hosts.

00:16:47.720 --> 00:16:52.559
The whole earth is full of his glory.

00:16:52.559 --> 00:16:55.559
And the post of the door moved the voice of him

00:16:55.559 --> 00:17:00.559
that cried and the house was filled with smoke.

00:17:00.640 --> 00:17:03.799
I'll reference this passage again in just a moment,

00:17:03.799 --> 00:17:05.760
but I want you to understand that here

00:17:05.760 --> 00:17:07.679
in this text of scripture,

00:17:08.519 --> 00:17:11.000
Isaiah has this proper view of God.

00:17:11.000 --> 00:17:16.000
The king Uzziah has died and we find that as Isaiah is there

00:17:16.440 --> 00:17:18.519
and this is what we would refer to as the call,

00:17:18.519 --> 00:17:21.559
the commission of Isaiah, in just a little while

00:17:21.559 --> 00:17:23.640
he would say, here am I, send me.

00:17:23.640 --> 00:17:26.000
And we understand that what led to him being

00:17:26.000 --> 00:17:28.880
