that we truly would come to that place where we'd say, without him, I can do nothing.

00:46:37.179 --> 00:46:43.420
Who then is Paul? I mean, who are we? We're just ministers. We're just servants. I'm thankful that

00:46:43.420 --> 00:46:48.300
I'm saved by the grace of God and that I'm a joint heir with Jesus Christ. Hallelujah. I mean,

00:46:48.300 --> 00:46:53.020
praise the Lord for what he's done. And we find here this morning that it's something that we

00:46:53.020 --> 00:47:00.059
have to do individually. Humble yourselves. And let me just finish with one thought from the life

00:47:00.059 --> 00:47:09.500
of Nebuchadnezzar. If you don't humble yourself, God is able to abase you, to humble you. And I

00:47:09.500 --> 00:47:17.260
would submit to you this morning that it is far better, far better to humble yourself than to be

00:47:17.260 --> 00:47:25.820
humbled by God. After Nebuchadnezzar lived out in the field as an animal for those years,

00:47:27.580 --> 00:47:31.580
it's recorded in Daniel 4 in verse 37 at the last part of the verse,

00:47:31.580 --> 00:47:40.619
and those that walk in pride, he is able to abase. He experienced that firsthand.

00:47:41.580 --> 00:47:46.940
And I would say to you this morning, I don't want to experience that. It'd be far better

00:47:47.820 --> 00:47:55.100
for us to take heed to what James says in chapter 4 in verse 10, to humble ourselves. It'd be far

00:47:55.100 --> 00:48:01.660
better for us to take the truth of 1 Peter chapter 5 in verse 5 and be clothed with humility.

00:48:02.619 --> 00:48:12.619
Because if we walk in pride, as Nebuchadnezzar learned so, so well, he, God, is able to abase.

00:48:13.660 --> 00:48:20.619
And I hope this morning that we would take heed, that we would humble ourselves, truly get to that

00:48:20.619 --> 00:48:27.020
place where we say, Lord, help me to identify the pride. Help me to root it out. Help me to keep

00:48:27.580 --> 00:48:33.580
the proper view of who you are. Help me not to get distracted. Help me not to hear those

00:48:33.580 --> 00:48:38.940
compliments and get a big head, get full of myself and think I'm something, because I know,

00:48:38.940 --> 00:48:44.140
God, without you, I'm nothing. Let us pray together. Father, we love you this morning.

00:48:44.140 --> 00:48:49.260
We thank you so much for loving us. I thank you for the truth of thy word, and I thank you for

00:48:49.500 --> 00:48:58.299
your grace in our lives. God, we see all around us pride, and so often, as I mentioned throughout

00:48:58.299 --> 00:49:05.260
the message, it's easy for us to identify the pride in the lives of others. But this morning,

00:49:05.260 --> 00:49:09.979
as we study your word, we're challenged individually and personally as your children to

00:49:10.780 --> 00:49:17.179
to humble ourselves. And God, I pray that you would help each one of us to

00:49:18.619 --> 00:49:23.419
identify and root out pride in our lives, that we'd understand that we'll never have a proper

00:49:23.419 --> 00:49:29.580
view of ourselves until we first have a proper view of you. And God, I thank you that you are

00:49:29.580 --> 00:49:34.619
high, holy, and lifted up. I thank you that you are the Lord God omnipotent and that you reign.

00:49:35.500 --> 00:49:42.299
I thank you that you're the vine. We're just the branches. I thank you that we have the opportunity,

00:49:42.299 --> 00:49:49.099
as Paul mentions in 1 Corinthians 3, to be laborers together with thee. But we recognize

00:49:49.099 --> 00:49:55.179
that we're just ministers. We're just servants. God, I pray that you'd help us to walk in humility,

00:49:56.220 --> 00:50:00.220
that we would take the truth of thy word, and that we'd walk

00:50:00.220 --> 00:50:05.820
humbly with our God, that your grace might continue to flow in our lives,

00:50:05.820 --> 00:50:10.020
that you would not resist us because we walk in pride.

00:50:10.020 --> 00:50:14.820
Help us, Lord, to take heed this morning to the truth of thy word.

00:50:14.820 --> 00:50:19.320
I pray that decisions would be made throughout this place, Lord,

00:50:19.320 --> 00:50:23.320
that would bring honor and glory to thy name alone.

00:50:23.320 --> 00:50:25.620
For it's in Christ's name we do pray.

00:50:25.620 --> 00:50:26.520
Would you stand with me?

00:50:26.520 --> 00:50:29.020
Heads are bowed, eyes are closed.

00:50:29.020 --> 00:50:31.020
At the end of each of our services, we have an invitation.

00:50:31.020 --> 00:50:33.520
We're given an opportunity to respond.

00:50:33.520 --> 00:50:35.720
And this morning, maybe the Lord spoke to your heart.

00:50:35.720 --> 00:50:39.820
Maybe you'll be honest before the Lord and say, as best I know,

00:50:39.820 --> 00:50:41.120
I'm walking in humility.

00:50:41.120 --> 00:50:45.020
But maybe you want to come and ask God to help you to stay in that place.

00:50:45.020 --> 00:50:52.920
Because it's amazing how quickly pride can creep up in the lives of individuals.

00:50:52.920 --> 00:50:56.420
And as Kimberly plays the piano, the altar will be open.

00:50:56.420 --> 00:50:59.420
And maybe you're not saved this morning, not sure of heaven.

00:50:59.420 --> 00:51:03.220
If you were to die today, you're not 100% sure that heaven is your home.

00:51:03.220 --> 00:51:05.220
If that's you this morning, we'd ask you to come.

00:51:05.220 --> 00:51:08.920
We'll take a Bible and show you how you can know for sure that heaven is your home.

00:51:08.920 --> 00:51:10.920
As Kimberly plays, the altar is open.

